\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The O-ISAC paradigm evolution. (A) RF-ISAC systems in sub-6 GHz/mmWave bands often face deployment-constrained spectrum and hardware limits, motivating a transition toward photonic carriers to pursue Tb/s-class capacity and millimeter-scale sensing targets. (B) Optical ISAC leverages the broad photonic spectrum ($\approx 28.3$--845 THz), with implementations clustering in operational windows (telecom for fiber and NIR/visible/photonic-THz for wireless). (C) The review taxonomy branches Optical ISAC into fiber-based, free-space/photonic-THz, and VLC/LiFi modalities, each characterized by distinct signal models and dominant impairments.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:intro-paradigm}{{1}{3}{}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {I}{\ignorespaces Axis-Based Comparison of This Review with Existing Related Review- and Survey-Style Works}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:intro-related}{{I}{3}{}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces RF-ISAC vs. O-ISAC Performance Comparison}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:intro-rf-vs-optical}{{II}{3}{}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Physical mechanisms behind the three competitive advantages of O-ISAC. (Left) Capacity scaling is achieved via dense multiplexing (WDM/SDM), enabling aggregate rates of 241.85 Tb/s in wired systems [O-ISAC-046] and dense parallel channels in wireless settings [O-ISAC-021]. (Center) Sensing precision is driven by ultra-wide effective bandwidth, enabling wireless range resolution down to $\Delta r_{\min } = 2.5$ mm and $\mathrm  {CRQ}_{\Delta } = 4.8\times 10^{13}$ bps/m (480 Gb/s/cm) [O-ISAC-105]. (Right) Spatial isolation is inherent to narrow optical beams, reducing multi-user interference and RF-EMI susceptibility compared to wide RF sectors.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:intro-advantages}{{2}{4}{}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Unified taxonomy of O-ISAC modalities derived from a systematic PRISMA-compliant analysis of 220 primary studies (2020--2025). (Top-left) Fiber O-ISAC leverages DAS/DSCM infrastructure for long-haul sensing and Tb/s-class data transmission. (Top-right) Free-space optical O-ISAC targets outdoor inter-building links with coherent detection and atmospheric compensation. (Bottom-left) VLC O-ISAC supports indoor lighting, connectivity, and sub-centimeter positioning. (Bottom-right) Photonic THz O-ISAC bridges optical and wireless THz domains to achieve the highest reported $\mathrm  {CRQ}_{\Delta }$ metrics, exceeding 100 Gb/s/cm, i.e., $1.0\times 10^{13}$ bps/m.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:intro-taxonomy}{{3}{4}{}{figure.3}{}}
